---
description: LTR, RTL and bidirectional content rules
alwaysApply: false
---
When working on webpage content:
- Preserve explicit HTML dir attributes.
- Respect element-level direction.
- Use lang as metadata.
- Account for CSS direction, text-align and unicode-bidi.
- Support mixed LTR/RTL content.
- Do not assume a page is uniformly RTL.
- Keep numbers, URLs, punctuation and Latin fragments readable inside RTL text.
- Prefer logical CSS properties.
- Keep application UI direction separate from crawled-page direction.
- Test rendering and inline editing.
